---

Acoustic-mesh is an independent experimental multi-device acoustic-mesh engineering repository. It contains WebRTC peer-connection, visualization, signal-processing, and graph-aggregation work where implemented.

Historical/project-local ecosystem references include DGAF-Framework, PDMAL, Driftwatch, the Schizophonic Studio vocabulary, and phi-harmonic analysis concepts. Those references do not establish inherited governance authority, certification, production readiness, physical acoustic performance, cognitive measurement, or empirical validity.

Current claims about this repository are bounded by its own source, tests, CI, and dated evidence. Cross-repository status does not transfer automatically.

Related repositories:
  - DGAF-Framework: https://github.com/ndrorchestration/DGAF-Framework
  - Driftwatch: https://github.com/ndrorchestration/Driftwatch
  - 3d-visualization-hub: https://github.com/ndrorchestration/3d-visualization-hub

